  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "I'm sorry to hear that you're experiencing this. Feeling emotionally numb can be a complex and challenging experience. Here are some steps you might consider taking to help manage and understand your feelings:\n\n1. **Seek Support**: Talking to someone you trust, such as a friend, family member, or a mental health professional, can be very helpful. Sometimes just sharing your feelings can make a big difference.\n\n2. **Mindfulness and Meditation**: Practicing mindfulness or meditation can help you become more aware of your emotions and thoughts. Even a few minutes a day can make a difference.\n\n3. **Physical Activity**: Exercise can boost your mood and help you feel more connected to your body and your emotions. It doesn't have to be intense; even a short walk can be beneficial.\n\n4. **Healthy Lifestyle Choices**: Eating well, getting enough sleep, and avoiding excessive alcohol or drugs can all impact your emotional state.\n\n5. **Journaling**: Writing down your thoughts and feelings can help you understand them better and process your emotions.\n\n6. **Limit Screen Time**: Reducing time spent on social media and other screens can help you avoid comparing yourself to others and reduce feelings of isolation.\n\n7. **Professional Help**: If you find that your feelings of numbness are persistent and affecting your daily life, it might be helpful to speak with a mental health professional who can provide guidance and support.\n\nRemember, it's okay to seek help and take time to heal. You're not alone, and there are resources available to support you.",
